  "description": "Find the Nth magical number divisible by either A or B. We use binary search on the result range.",
  "target": 4,
  "pseudocode": "1. low = min(A, B), high = N * min(A, B)\n2. while low < high:\n3.   mid = low + floor((high - low) / 2)\n4.   count = floor(mid/A) + floor(mid/B) - floor(mid/lcm(A,B))\n5.   if count < N: low = mid + 1\n6.   else: high = mid\n7. return low",
